(
        '21960',
        'EU Sanctions List Discrepancies Errors',
        'EU Sanctions List Discrepancies Errors',
        'Dear @Mohammed Attallah,    Based on our web session, please find our response to each point provided from your end, highlighted in blue:     1. Significant and unexplained increase in list entries: Approximately 1,000 new entries are being added daily, despite no corresponding additions being published by the EU sanctions list.     Our Response: After our investigation, it appears that the increase is related to updates made to the AKA names associated with existing records on the list. These newly added aliases have contributed to the increase in the total number of entries.     AML Team Response: Kindly provide us with the proposed solution for the reported issue, as it is directly impacting the delta screening process. Please note that an illogical number of alerts is being generated on a daily basis, which requires urgent attention and resolution.    Pio-Tech response: Please note that this matter should not be considered a system issue. Based on our investigation, the additional entries are related to AKA (Alias) names introduced through updates published in the official EU sanctions list and are not generated from our side. As you are aware, the EU list is considered a free-source list, and updates to aliases associated with existing entities may occur frequently. Consequently, such changes can lead to an increase in the number of records processed during the delta screening activity.    2. Missing names from the list: The following are examples of names that do not appear in the system:  ? PJSC Slavneft Megionneftegaz  ? LLC Slavneft Krasnoyarskneftegaz  ? Joint-Stock Company “Optical-Mechanical Design Bureau”     Our Response: After checking the names provided, please be informed that we could not find the following names in the EU full list:  • PJSC Slavneft Megionneftegaz  • LLC Slavneft Krasnoyarskneftegaz     Kindly double-check the spelling and the approach used when searching for these names, and provide us with additional details so that we can investigate further.     Regarding "Joint-Stock Company ''Optical-Mechanical Design Bureau''", please be informed that this name is listed as an alias for "JSC OKB ASTRON" and it’s appear on the system, as shown in the picture below, which was extracted from the list.    AML Team Response: Please find attached the relevant files extracted from the official EU XML files for your reference.  Regarding “Joint-Stock Company ‘Optical-Mechanical Design Bureau’”, could you please clarify why the name does not appear in the system when searching using its alias?  Pio-Tech response :Regarding the names shared, please be informed that the issue was related to the handling of special characters during the name search process. The issue has been resolved after applying the necessary modifications, and the names will appear in the system by tomorrow morning as these changes require restarting the similarity engine.    As agreed with @Mohammed Attallah, and to avoid any interruption to your business operations, the restart process will be performed at 12:30 AM. @Mohammad Al-Katry will proceed with this task and confirm that all services are functioning as expected following the restart.    For "Joint-Stock Company ''Optical-Mechanical Design Bureau''", please note that this name is classified as an AKA (Alias) name and not as the main name listed in the EU sanctions list. Therefore, it is expected to appear under the details of the corresponding main record rather than as an independent primary entry in the system. Please note that the search process is performed based on the main name maintained in the sanctions list. Therefore, AKA (Alias) names can be viewed within the details of the corresponding main record after searching using the primary listed name.',
        '2026-06-08T00:00:00.000Z'::timestamptz,
