        '22014',
        'ODI Issue After Antivirus Upgrade',
        'ODI Issue After Antivirus Upgrade',
        'Dear Samar,    Based on our web session, kindly find below the status:      • Issue Reported by the customer: ODI Issue After Antivirus Upgrade.    • Status: Solved.    • Problem description: An issue was reported whereby Oracle Data Integrator (ODI) Studio and the ODI Agent could not be opened following a recent Kaspersky antivirus upgrade.    Root Cause:  The Kaspersky upgrade affected the Java Development Kit (JDK) installation/configuration on the server. As a result, the Java executables were no longer accessible (removed by the antivirus), preventing ODI from locating a valid JDK and causing both ODI Studio and the ODI Agent to fail during startup.              • Action Taken – recommended solution: Based on our web session, the issue has been resolved by installing and configuring a supported Java Development Kit (JDK 17.0.12). After updating the Java environment, ODI Studio and the ODI Agent started successfully and are now functioning normally.    To prevent the issue from recurring, kindly ensure that the Java installation path is excluded from antivirus scans, as the issue may re-occur in the following scenarios:    1- If the antivirus performs scheduled scans (for example, every 4 hours or at any predefined interval).  2- If the antivirus receives a new update.  3- If the server is restarted and the antivirus re-scans system files.    Kindly check from your side and confirm to close this ticket.     Best Regards,',
