        'Vulnerability Remediation on Server (IIB-BI-APP-live)',
        'Dear Pio-Tech Team,    During a recent security assessment, multiple vulnerabilities and compliance issues were identified on our IIB-BI-APP-live server.  As our system vendor, please prepare to perform the following hardening and remediation steps on the specified ports:  1.Tomcat Version Upgrade (Port 8080): Our current version is detected as Apache Tomcat/9.0.74_SAP Support Pack / Patch Upgrade. Please upgrade the system to Apache Tomcat version 9.0.86 or later to address known security risks.  2.TLS Protocol Hardening (Port 3389): Enable support for TLS 1.2 and/or 1.3, and disable support for TLS 1.1 (as well as any older versions) to ensure secure connections.  3.Removal of Default Tomcat Files (Port 8080): The remote web server currently contains default files. Please delete the default index page and remove the example JSP and servlets. Additionally, follow Tomcat or OWASP best practices to replace or modify the default error page.  Operational Impact Assessment: Before deploying any of these changes, upgrades, or patches to production, please review and discuss with us any potential operational impact, compatibility issues, or service disruptions regarding Ports 8080 and 3389.  Kindly provide us with your technical assessment and confirmation. Once we review and approve it, we will give you the green light to proceed with the implementation so we can re-scan and validate .',
