(
        '22057',
        'ETL failure on the old server caused by the index PIO_STOP_PAYMENTS.CUS_NUM_LF.”',
        'Dear Team,    We have an ETL failure on the Old sybase system for the past few days. Could you please fix the issue and load the missing dates data from new production.    Also please be informed we will be stopping the load on old servers after this quarter end (Jun 2026) therefore to ensure all data is loaded till quarter end we need your assistance.',
        'Dear Mahin,    Based on our web session, kindly find below the status:      • Issue Reported by the customer: ETL failure on the old server caused by the index PIO_STOP_PAYMENTS.CUS_NUM_LF.    -Note: Based on the trace performed, the issue was not related to the PIO_STOP_PAYMENTS.CUS_NUM_LF index. The root cause was insufficient free space in the Sybase IQ database DBSpace BANKBI_Main. The false reference to the ticket title originated because the bank raised the issue in an older ticket, which caused the confusion.    • Status: Solved.    • Problem description: The ETL daily job on the old production server had been falling since June 18, 2026, because the Sybase IQ BANKBI_Main DBSpace had run out of available storage space, preventing the ETL process from completing successfully.                          • Action Taken – recommended solution: Based on our web session, kindly be informed that the issue was resolved after additional data files were added to the BANKBI_Main DBSpace from your side. Following this, the ETL daily fill job was re-executed from the point of failure for the date June 23, 2026, and completed successfully, Furthermore, as discussed over the phone, the subsequent ETL daily fill job also completed successfully without any issues.         Kindly check from your side and confirm to close this ticket.     Best Regards,',
