(
        '22072',
        'Request for transactions Log and Root Cause of Zero Alert Generation for Frequent Inbound/Outbound Transactions within 30 days',
        'Dear Technical Support Team,    I am writing to raise an urgent technical and compliance issue regarding our AML system.    We have detected that the following scenario has not generated any alerts since December 31, 2024, until today, despite being displayed as "Active" on the system interface:        Scenario: Frequent Inbound/Outbound Transactions within 30 days (Individual Customers).    Considering our transaction volume, having zero alerts for this critical scenario over this extended period is statistically impossible and exposes us to high compliance risks.    To resolve this immediately, we strictly request the following:        Full Audit Trail & Change Logs: Please provide the comprehensive historical logs for this specific scenario from 30-12-2024 to present. We need to verify if any modifications, code changes, or parameter tuning (Thresholds/Criteria) were applied that caused this suppression.        System & Rule Engine Investigation: A deep-dive investigation into why the rule engine is failing to trigger alerts. Please confirm if the individual transaction data feeds (Data Lineage) are properly reaching this scenario.  Please treat this ticket with High Priority and provide us with the requested logs and an initial root-cause analysis within 24 hours.    Thank you for your prompt cooperation',
        'Dear      Based on our web session, kindly find below the status:     • Issue Reported by the customer: Request for transactions Log and Root Cause of Zero Alert Generation for Frequent Inbound/Outbound Transactions within 30 days.    • Category: Client Action Required     • Status: Solved.     • Problem description: Issue with LTG code of the scenario .     • Action Taken – recommended solution: Based on our web session, please note that after the alerts for the scenario were generated, it was requested from your side to deactivate the scenario and delete the related alerts until the rule logic is corrected from your side    Kindly check and confirm so we may proceed with closing the ticket.',
