        '22062',
        'Study vulnerabilities',
        'approciate your help in resolving the attached VAs',
        'Dear @Bilal Jabr,    Please find below the status of the reported vulnerabilities on the ETL production environment:    1. CVE-2025-66614: *21- False positive. Client certificates are not used at the connector level with the Tomcat bundled with BusinessObjects.  2. CVE-2026-24733: *22- Not impacted. The HTTP HEAD method (doHead) is not in use in our environment.  3. Multiple CVEs (CVE-2025-6021,CVE-2025-6052,CVE-2025-47183,CVE-2025-47219,CVE-2025-7424,CVE-2025-7425,CVE-2025-8732,CVE-2025-43342,CVE-2025-43356,CVE-2025-43272,CVE-2025-43368,CVE-2025-10911,CVE-2026-21925,CVE-2026-21932,CVE-2026-21933,CVE-2026-21945,CVE-2026-21947): According to SAP Note 3710568, these vulnerabilities are planned to be addressed in SAP Bundle Patch (SBP) 202602 (February 2026), subject to the general restrictions described in SAP Note 2918418 – Oracle Critical Patch Updates for SAP.  4. CVE-2025-68493: It is recommended to upgrade BI/IPS to version 4.3 to address this vulnerability.',
