        '22230',
        'Applying encryption on database level',
        'We would like to understand the whether enabling database-level encryption could have any impact on GOAML functionality, performance, data integrity or other application behavior.   1- Is database-level encryption fully supported from PIO-Tech support?  2- Could database-level encryption have any impact on GOAML batch execution performance?  3- Could database-level encryption have any impact on data integrity or consistency within GOAML?  4- Could it impact data loading, ETL processing, or data extraction?  5- Could it affect database indexing, query performance or optimizer behavior?  6- Are there any known limitations, unsupported configurations, or PIO-Tech recommendations regarding database-level encryption for GOAML?  6- Does PIO-Tech recommend against encryption specific PIO-Tech database objects or tables?  8- Are there any documented performance benchmarks or best practices for enabling database-level encryption in GOAML production Environments?  9- Have you encountered any customer cases where database-level encryption caused issues with GOAML functionality or performance?   10- If database-level encryption is not recommended or is unsupported for GOAML, could you please confirm this explicitly and provide the technical reason or the relevant PIO-Tech documentation supporting this recommendation?',
